# TypeScript & Workers

Apply when editing `src/**/*.ts`. Read [doc/stack.md](../../doc/stack.md) for layout and commands. Subagent: `build-agent`.

## Structure

Follow `layout` in `doc/stack.md`. Default (Workers):

- `src/core` — orchestration, routing, handlers
- `src/services` — external integrations
- `src/utils` — pure helpers
- `src/types/` — shared contracts

Prefer small, single-purpose functions. Match existing logging patterns.

## Types & docs

- Type-annotate functions and methods
- Public APIs: English JSDoc when non-obvious

## Naming

Full rules: [doc/coding-conventions.md](../../doc/coding-conventions.md).

| Target | Case | Example |
|--------|------|---------|
| Variables, functions, methods | lowerCamelCase | `userName`, `fetchOrder` |
| Classes, interfaces, types, enums | PascalCase | `UserService`, `OrderStatus` |
| Module constants | SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE | `MAX_RETRY_COUNT` |
| Enum members | PascalCase | `OrderStatus.Pending` |
| General module files | kebab-case | `user-service.ts` |
| React component files | PascalCase | `UserProfile.tsx` |

Semantics (all stacks): verb-first functions; `is`/`has`/`can` booleans; plural collections; English identifiers only.

## Workers specifics

- Keep handler signatures stable unless systemspec changes
- Bindings must match `wrangler.toml` and docs
- Validate auth on triggers/webhooks; fail closed
- No secrets in logs

## Before finishing

Use quality commands from `doc/stack.md` (`test_single`, `typecheck`).
